From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the full-grab tap lets the escape combo through to OmacVM Gestures

Applies after omacvm-cocoa-shortcuts-logic.patch (omacvm_is_escape_combo),
omacvm-cocoa-system-shortcuts.patch (which includes its header) and
omacvm-cocoa-keys-for-macos.patch.

What: QEMU's full-grab event tap returns the escape combo (Ctrl+Option+Esc;
through 3.0.x also the old Ctrl+Option+Cmd+Esc; exactly these modifiers)
unhandled, key down and key up, instead of sending it to the guest.

Why: a new event tap goes to the head of the HID chain. A VM started after
OmacVM Gestures put QEMU's tap ahead of Gestures': QEMU sent the combo to the
guest and swallowed it, so the way out of the full-screen VM did nothing
(PR #39). Gestures creates its tap again when a VM comes to the front, but a
combo pressed before that, or any other order, still went to the guest. Now
the order does not matter: whichever tap comes first, Gestures gets it. When
Gestures is not running the combo reaches our window the normal way, where
omacvm-cocoa-system-shortcuts.patch's fallback hands the keyboard back to
macOS in full screen (in a window it goes to the VM as before).

Upstream: not applicable (OmacVM's helpers).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-shortcuts.sh (which keys are the combo,
and that no macOS shortcut is); the build checks the patch is in
ui/cocoa.m; src/gestures/mac/test-escape.c (Gestures' side, no QEMU).

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -688,6 +688,23 @@
         return cgEvent;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * OmacVM: the escape combo (ui/omacvm-shortcuts.h) is OmacVM Gestures'.
+     * A VM started after Gestures puts this tap ahead of Gestures' in the
+     * chain, so this tap lets the combo through instead of sending it to the
+     * guest: Gestures' tap takes it next, whichever came first. Without
+     * Gestures it reaches our window the normal way (handleEventLocked).
+     */
+    if (type == kCGEventKeyDown || type == kCGEventKeyUp) {
+        CGEventFlags flags = CGEventGetFlags(cgEvent);
+        if (omacvm_is_escape_combo(
+                (int)CGEventGetIntegerValueField(cgEvent, kCGKeyboardEventKeycode),
+                flags & kCGEventFlagMaskControl, flags & kCGEventFlagMaskAlternate,
+                flags & kCGEventFlagMaskCommand, flags & kCGEventFlagMaskShift)) {
+            return cgEvent;
+        }
+    }
+
     NSEvent *event = [NSEvent eventWithCGEvent:cgEvent];
     if ([view isKeyboardCaptured] && [view handleEvent:event]) {
         COCOA_DEBUG("Global events tap: qemu handled the event, capturing!\n");
